[center][size=5][b]NO PLOT ARMOR[/b][/size][/center]
[center][size=3]Killable Story NPCs and Dismemberment[/size][/center]
[quote][b]BEFORE YOU INSTALL[/b] [b]Killing quest NPCs can permanently break quests.[/b] That is the entire point of this mod, so use a disposable manual save, never your main one. [b]Spawns are copies.[/b] Shooting a spawned Judy or Panam does nothing to the real one. [b]Still being proven.[/b] Killability and the spawner are stable in game; gore on custom outfits is freshly validated and I want your reports. If a specific NPC or outfit won't lose limbs, report it with the record name and whether it was spawned or quest-owned.[/quote]
[line]
[heading]FEATURES[/heading]
[b][u]Killability[/u][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Protected NPCs die.[/b] The mortal override replaces immortal and invulnerable states while NPCs are attached, and late quest-added protections are stripped as they appear. [/*]
[*][b]Friendly fire connects.[/b] Your attacks carry FriendlyFire plus immortality-ignore flags from creation through the damage pipeline, and the aimed-at friendly NPC is briefly neutralized so bullets collide instead of ghosting through. [/*]
[*][b]Vanilla rules kept where they matter.[/b] Nonlethal hits and fist-fight hits use the game's original conditions and will not kill. [/*]
[*][b]Master switch.[/b] [i]Enable No Plot Armor[/i] (on by default) controls every gameplay hook. Turning it off restores protection overrides and fire blocks. The setting persists in [b]enabled.txt[/b]. [/*]
[/list]
[b][u]Gore[/u][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Dismemberment for story NPCs.[/b] Wound data is injected into appearances that ship with none, so Judy, Panam, Rogue, River, Lizzy Wizzy, Reed, Songbird and the rest can actually come apart. [/*]
[*][b]Custom outfits work.[/b] Any woundless NPC appearance gets body-type-matched wounds automatically, including outfit and body mods. Load order doesn't matter; appearances that already have wounds (yours or another dismemberment mod's) are left alone. [/*]
[*][b]No archive needed.[/b] The mod seeds itself from vanilla gang bodies at startup. The 0.2.0 download is code only, about 23KB. [/*]
[*][b]Living limbs.[/b] Ongoing limb loss on living NPCs is Relentless Live Dismember's department, not this mod's. It pairs well with it, details below. [/*]
[/list]
[b][u]Spawner & tools[/u][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Story-character spawner.[/b] 221 records with a searchable catalog and a featured list. Copies spawn two meters in front of you, tagged so one button removes them all, including tags from the mod's older names. [/*]
[*][b]NPCs retaliate when hit[/b] [i](off by default)[/i]. A living NPC you hit turns hostile. Attitude is only attitude, so AI and scenes still decide what they actually do. Persists in [b]retaliation.txt[/b]. [/*]
[*][b]Inspect NPC in crosshairs.[/b] Prints health, protection and god-mode sources, flesh and cyber limb counts, and hit/gore counters. This is the single most useful thing you can paste in a bug report. [/*]
[*][b]Verbose logging[/b] [i](off by default)[/i]. Turn it on only for bug reports. It persists in [b]verbose.txt[/b]. [/*]
[/list]
[line]
[heading]REQUIREMENTS & INSTALLATION[/heading]
[b]Required:[/b] Cyberpunk 2077 2.x, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]redscript[/url] (RED4ext comes with it). [b]Find your game folder[/b] In Steam, right-click [b]Cyberpunk 2077 > Manage > Browse local files[/b]. You want the folder containing [b]r6[/b] and [b]bin[/b]. [b]Vortex (recommended)[/b] Install [b]NoPlotArmor-0.2.0.zip[/b] via [b]Install From File[/b] and deploy. The ZIP has [b]r6/[/b] and [b]bin/[/b] at its root, so Vortex maps them straight into the game. [b]Manual[/b] Extract the ZIP into the game folder and merge when prompted. [b]Check that it's running[/b] Open the CET overlay in game. You should see a [b]No Plot Armor v0.2.0[/b] window. Spawn a record, then press [b]Inspect NPC in crosshairs[/b] on it.
[spoiler][b]Updating[/b] Extract the newer ZIP the same way and overwrite. Your [b]enabled.txt[/b], [b]retaliation.txt[/b] and [b]verbose.txt[/b] live next to the mod and are not overwritten. [b]Uninstalling[/b] Vortex: disable or remove the mod there. Manual: delete [b]r6/scripts/NoPlotArmor/[/b] and [b]bin/x64/plugins/cyber_engine_tweaks/mods/NoPlotArmor/[/b]. Leftover folders from the old names ([b]r6/scripts/NPCOmegaGore/[/b], [b].../mods/NPCOmegaGore/[/b], [b].../mods/OmegaNPC/[/b]) can be deleted too.[/spoiler]
[line]
[heading]COMPATIBILITY[/heading]
[b][u]Works alongside[/u][/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/24210]GoreRunner (Blood and Carnage Overhaul)[/url]: gibs, blood, remade gore models. This mod decides [i]whether[/i] story NPCs can come apart; GoreRunner decides how nasty it looks. [/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35703]RELENTLESS - Live Dismemberment[/url]: limbs off living enemies. Recommended if you want crawl-and-keep-fighting instead of corpse-only gore. [/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/36454]Civilian Dismemberment (Collateral Damage)[/url]: the WoundInject technique this mod's injection is built on. Files that already have wounds are left alone, so whichever mod gets there first wins. [/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/28411]Use Weapons and Quick Slots Everywhere[/url]: draw and shoot in safe zones with no Action Blocked popup. [/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/10946]Gameplay Restrictions - UNLOCKED[/url]: sprint, jump and dodge in safe areas and while carrying bodies. Movement layer; no fight with the weapons mod above. [/*]
[/list]
[b][u]Known conflicts and caveats[/u][/b]
[quote][b]Quest logic:[/b] this mod ignores and bypasses safe zones, quest protections and forced empty-hands states. That CAN and WILL break quests. Manual save, separate from your main one. [b]Other dismemberment mods:[/b] an appearance that already has wounds keeps them; this mod only fills in the ones that have none. [b]Friendly-fire workaround:[/b] fast target switching or delayed projectiles can still miss; incidental hits on friendlies outside the crosshair are not guaranteed.[/quote]
[line]
[heading]CREDITS & SOURCE[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Appearance Menu Mod public catalog[/b] — the character record list is derived from it. [/*]
[*][b]Collateral Damage (Cazanu)[/b] — the WoundInject donor pattern this mod's injection is adapted from. [/*]
[*][b]Cazanu[/b] — GoreRunner and RELENTLESS, the two mods this one is built to sit between. [/*]
[*][b]RaMsOc2 and EGG[/b] — the safe-zone and restriction mods in the pairing stack above. [/*]
[/list]
[b]Source code:[/b] GitHub repo link follows with the 0.2.0 release ([b]MIT[/b] for the scripts; game assets belong to CD PROJEKT RED).
